    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40c8186f_6f119850",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/PermissionMonitor.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 86,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059499
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-28T00:18:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lorenzo originally suggested moving the logic here (https://googleplex-android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/5980122/1/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java#5227). \n\nI can move this functionality to a separate class / VPN.java, there is a small caveat that during package installation, the new class will need to call into PermissionMonitor after PermissionMonitor has updated its knowledge of the new uid\u0027s permission, so we are effectively introducing an implicit timing constraint between the two\u0027s interaction, which could cause subtle bugs. \n\nLorenzo/Chalard, WDYT about moving the new logic out of PermissionMonitor?",
      "parentUuid": "ad8f8b7b_8f68d456",
      "revId": "40d6cc4d4163f8c5dbfd6066424aad169246b816",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
