      "writtenOn": "2019-02-22T02:30:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a bit bullish about the naming because \"intersect\" has a common, specific meaning that designates exactly 1 + 2. Because of this I wouldn\u0027t expect an \"intersectUids\" method to also perform 3 and 4.\nThis can be solved by touching up the name, or having a separate filtering method, or even judicious comments on the call sites to signal the slightly unusual semantics. In this case I tend to think the separate method is best, as there doesn\u0027t seem to be any performance concerns with it :\n\nuids \u003d intersectUids(...)\nuids.remove {appId -\u003e mApps.getOrDefault(appId, NETWORK) !\u003d SYSTEM}\nuids.remove(vpnAppUid)",
